# How many jobs an id stands for: a Slurm bracket its tasks, any other id one.
# 0 means it is no id, and the record gate skips it: the anchor cannot say
# a<=b or step>0, and a bracket counted 0 or 1 would be a wrong number nobody
# can see is wrong.  Each term is ONE anchored match, because a split on "-"
# then ":" lets gawk read "12:2" as 12 and count 0-12:2 as 13.
