# ---- COMPACT: which section a row is in, and what fits the screen ----------
# Sections: 1 stuck, 2 blocked on nodes, 3 held by admin, 4 pending, 5 running,
# 6 other live states (COMPLETING, SUSPENDED, ...).  Only a CLOSED list of reasons
# is ordinary waiting; any other pending reason is stuck, so a reason sq does not
# know stays visible instead of vanishing into "… n jobs pending".  Whole-string
# equality on %r, never a prefix: "Dependency" must not swallow
# "DependencyNeverSatisfied".  A prefix is safe only on the visible side, which
# only names the category: a cluster fault is "blocked on nodes", a hold that
# needs an admin (a launch failure Slurm requeued held, or a job it requeued
# in held state) "held by admin".
function jclass(st, why) {
  if (st == "R")  return 5
  if (st != "PD") return 6
